    <div>
      <h2 class="section-title">How it<br>works</h2>
      <p class="callout">The School does not stop at describing a problem. A question is built, placed in a room, and watched.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="divider"></div>
  <div class="method-steps fade-up">
    <div class="method-step">
      <span class="t-label method-index">01</span>
      <h3 class="method-title">Speculative prototyping</h3>
      <p class="location-feature-desc">A prototype is a way of thinking. It can be rough, unstable or incomplete, as long as it makes the question physical.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-step">
      <span class="t-label method-index">02</span>
      <h3 class="method-title">Making and experimentation</h3>
      <p class="location-feature-desc">Research proceeds by assembling materials, running tests, breaking the setup and adjusting. Analysis develops alongside the object.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-step">
      <span class="t-label method-index">03</span>
      <h3 class="method-title">Participation and public testing</h3>
      <p class="location-feature-desc">Some experiments stay in the atelier. Others are opened to a public, a partner or a live situation to see how the system behaves when other bodies enter it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
